      "content": "No, don't start a high-dose vitamin K supplement — it directly counteracts warfarin and can destabilize your INR, raising your risk of clot or bleeding complications. The good news is you don't need a supplement: eating a consistent amount of vitamin K–rich foods (leafy greens) is fine and actually the recommended approach. If you want to adjust your diet or add any supplement, check with the doctor managing your warfarin first so your dose can be adjusted accordingly.",
