      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Yes, sticking to food sources is safer than a pill — the key isn't avoiding greens, it's keeping your intake *consistent* so your warfarin dose stays matched to it. There's no magic number to hit; the goal is roughly the same amount of leafy greens from week to week, not more or less. If you want to eat more spinach and kale than you currently do, that's fine, but mention it to your prescriber so they can check your INR and adjust your dose if needed.",
